v 3

d wooldid: Estimation of Difference-in-Differences Treatment Effects with Staggered Treatment Onset Using Heterogeneity-Robust Two-Way Fixed Effects Regressions
d
d Author: Thomas A. Hegland, Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality, thomas.hegland@ahrq.hhs.gov
d
d wooldid offers a set of tools for implementing difference-in-differences
d style analyses with staggered treatment onset using the two-way fixed
d effects approach proposed in Wooldridge (2025) and the high dimensional
d fixed effects estimators developed by Correia (2017). Features include
d estimation of various types of average treatment effects, comparison of
d treatment effects across subgroups, estimation of event study style
d estimates and related parallel trends assumption tests (including Roth
d (2022) pre-trend power diagnostics and a test that all event study
d effects lie on one line through the reference period), simultaneous
d confidence bands for event studies, estimation of average and marginal
d treatment effects in the presence of a continuous treatment (or
d treatment intensity) variable [experimental], anticipation windows, a
d cohort-by-relative-period effects table, replay of stored results, and a
d fast point-estimates-only mode. This suite also can produce event study
d plots, histograms of treatment effects by cohort, and plots of treatment
d effects across the distribution of a specified continuous treatment
d variable. Options for inference include standard analytic clustered
d standard errors, standard errors that account for sampling variation in
d covariates (unconditional standard errors), Ibragimov and Muller (2010)
d style cluster-robust inference, randomization (permutation) inference
d over the assignment of treatment onset for settings with few treated
d clusters, and cluster bootstrap inference in both a resampling and a
d Bayesian (Dirichlet reweighting) flavor, with percentile,
d bias-corrected, accelerated and studentized intervals.
d
d KW: difference-in-differences
d KW: did
d KW: twfe
d KW: staggered
d
d Requires: STATA 16, reghdfe version 5.7.3, ftools, gtools
d
d Optional packages: ppmlhdfe
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260819
d

